{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9005e5dcbdc3ef9c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n3\ttitle: Emit audit events for KServe inference requests with reliable at-least-once\n4\t  delivery\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n6\tcomponent: KServe\n7\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E001\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 6\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Emit audit events for KServe inference requests with reliable at-least-once delivery\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic implements inference audit logging in the KServe serving stack: every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits a structured audit event conforming to the published common audit event schema, and events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics that survive component restarts.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Emit one audit event per inference request through a KServe endpoint, capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status per the common audit event schema. No request or response payloads are recorded.\n40\t- Deliver audit events to the cluster audit sink (the standard cluster logging forwarder) with at-least-once semantics.\n41\t- Buffer or otherwise persist in-flight audit events so they are not lost when the emitting component restarts.\n42\t- Honor the per-project audit enablement contract: inference auditing emits events only for projects where it is enabled.\n43\t- Apply to both serverless and raw deployment modes of InferenceService, consistent with the platform's serving architecture.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- For a sample of inference requests against a KServe endpoint, each request produces an audit event containing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status, conforming to the published schema, with no payload data present in the event.\n48\t- With auditing enabled for a project, killing and restarting the emitting component mid-traffic results in no audit event loss (at-least-once delivery verified by comparing emitted requests against events received at the cluster audit sink).\n49\t- With auditing disabled for a project via the enablement contract, inference requests in that project produce no audit events; with it enabled, they do.\n50\t- Events arrive at the standard cluster logging forwarder and are structured (machine-parseable) per the schema.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-1 (P0): Every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status (not payloads).\n55\t- HLR-2 (P0): Audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart.\n56\t\n57\t## Risks / Notes\n58\t\n59\t- Delivery validation assumes the cluster audit sink (standard cluster logging forwarder) is available in the target cluster; if absent, HLR-2 validation cannot complete. This is an environment prerequisite, not a deliverable of this epic.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8651f2c66d4800a1","agent_id":"a2675c8e1f3ec1496","session_id":"ec977243-d2eb-4166-aef8-f740d35bd2a8","uuid":"91f59702-ffce-466a-ae6a-e24d0ceeedb9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:07:19.894Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9005e5dcbdc3ef9c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
