is persisted and reflected when the view is reloaded.\n46\t- The written state conforms to the per-project enablement contract and is observable by the inference audit emission path.\n47\t- A non-administrative user cannot change the per-project auditing setting.\n48\t- The control follows existing Dashboard conventions for project-scoped administration settings.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-3 (P1): Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8651f2c66d4800a1","agent_id":"a2675c8e1f3ec1496","session_id":"ec977243-d2eb-4166-aef8-f740d35bd2a8","uuid":"f4e626ab-f7ae-46a0-9ff4-2bfddea88cf8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:07:20.924Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80131fdf7b29a02a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
