mpact` fields are null and no epic lists an Investigation\nin dependencies, so no gating metadata issues exist.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nAll epics are Implementation type and correctly carry `ai_signals` (not\n`investigation_signals`); ai-signals files exist for all four epics. Every\nfrontmatter signal value matches its rationale file, and the rationales are\nconsistent with the strategy content: E001's greenfield contract scores\n(existing_foundation 0, adapter_pattern 0) fit schema-definition work; E002/E003\nscore pattern_precedent +1 and adapter_pattern +1 against the existing KServe\nrequest logger and Dashboard settings surfaces; E004's human_process_gates -1\ncorrectly reflects the docs editorial/technical review gates. E002's\nexternal_dependency 0 with the sink-availability caveat moved to a risk note is a\ndefensible coordination-vs-environment distinction. No signal contradicts the\nrubric conditions.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy, including a concrete\nkill-and-restart at-least-once verification for HLR-2 and an enable/disable\nbehavioral check for the per-project contract. Rule-mandated ACs: E004\n(docs-authoring) has the Rule 24 \"technically reviewed against implementation\" AC.\nRule 23 (rollback/feature-flag) does not apply — this is a new capability, not a\nreplacement. Rule 25 does not apply — no konflux chain. No AC is a misfiled\nschedule constraint, and no epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nAll strategy scope is covered: every HLR, the payload-exclusion constraint, the\nper-project enable/disable behavior, schema publication for future components, and\nboth serverless and raw deployment modes (diligently drawn from architecture\ncontext). Out-of-scope items are correctly excluded. Strategy-level context is\ncarried forward, not dropped: the audit-sink availability assumption is a risk note\non E002 and a Health Warning in the summary, and the strategy's missing sections\n(Impacted Teams, Dependencies, GWT ACs, NFRs) are explicitly flagged rather than\nsilently ignored. Minor nit: the problem statement's \"tamper-evident\" property\nappears in E001's scope (\"tamper-evident event content is representable\") but no\nepic's acceptance criteria verify it — see issues list.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23234,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8651f2c66d4800a1","agent_id":"a2675c8e1f3ec1496","session_id":"ec977243-d2eb-4166-aef8-f740d35bd2a8","uuid":"055c3374-dbc1-4a1e-997b-1f31bbf18f47","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:10:03.713Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
